  "slug": "codes-distance-49c0",
  "summary": "New tools target loss, leakage and circuit-level noise directly: loss-aware decoders, exact loss simulation, non-binary error models and GPU qLDPC decoding.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is modeling and decoding realistic circuit-level faults beyond i.i.d. Pauli noise. For qubit loss, Ellis uses frame-CSS certification to give exact, fast Pauli-frame shot sampling. A loss-aware CNN decoder with a fast sampler substantially reduces logical error rates for surface and high-rate qLDPC codes. Foliated surface codes are shown optimal against space- and time-like skip-gate leakage, outperforming SWAP-based circuits in stability. On the decoding side, non-binary detector error models merge Pauli error components to improve belief propagation. A GPU decoder for bivariate bicycle codes sustains one syndrome round per microsecond under circuit-level noise, with 120x throughput. A secondary thread concerns logical operations: code quilts enable ancilla-free fault-tolerant Pauli-product measurements between codeblocks. CSS-T-Product codes realize multi-qubit logical diagonal gates transversally, which enables tailored magic-state factories for algorithmic primitives.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
